{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-crankcase-extidle-single-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.41, step 7f: `process-crankcase-extidle-single`, THC, CO and NOx from EXTENDED IDLE (190, 290, 390) and from CRANKCASE EXTENDED IDLE (117, 217, 317) for the combination long-haul truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, from the default database plus the county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-hotelling.esm`).\n\nThe three extended-idle pollutant-processes are rated like 9190 -- hotelling hours, mode 200 at 1, hourFractionAdjust from the merged hotellingActivityDistribution at zone 261610, road type 1 -- with two adjustments energy did not need: NOx's humidity factor K (`rt_isNoxTotal` already named processes 90 and 91) and the diesel biodiesel fuel ratio for model years 1950-2006 (rows 7-9 of `gfb_*`). The crankcase three are CrankcaseEmissionCalculator's, `runspecchainedto` 117<-190, 217<-290, 317<-390: the parent times `crankcaseEmissionRatio`, and they live on their PARENT's road type, 1 (`rspp_chainRoadTypeID*`).\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 300: six blocks of 41 diesel and 9 CNG model years. `run_domainUnported` and `run_selectionUnported` are 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
